==English==
===Alternative forms===
* [[nay-sayer]]

===Etymology===
Origin: 1715–1725<!--http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/naysayer -->, from {{term|nay}} + {{suffix|say|er|lang=en}}, equivalent to {{suffix|naysay|er|lang=en}}. First recorded use: 1721<!--http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/naysayer -->.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈneɪ.ˌseɪ.ə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈneɪ.ˌseɪ.ɚ/|lang=en}}
*{{audio|en-us-naysayer.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|nay|say|er|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#One who consistently [[denies]], [[criticizes]], or [[doubts]]; a [[detractor]].
#:''He ignored the '''naysayers''' and succeeded with his idea.''

====Synonyms====
* [[pessimist]], [[doubter]], [[cynic]], [[misanthrope]]

====Antonyms====
* [[yeasayer]], [[yea-sayer]]

